-- STATUS: APPLIED 2026-08-04 against league_production
--
-- Reconstruct the 256 player_gamelogs rows the 8f4292e08 era repair left owned
-- by nobody. Each describes a real game that a rightful older player played,
-- was deleted from a modern same-name player's pid where it did not belong,
-- and was never written to the player who actually played it -- so the game
-- exists nowhere in player_gamelogs today.
--
-- This closes user:task/league/reconstruct-unowned-era-repair-gamelogs.md.
-- Its predecessor, user:task/league/close-out-era-falsifier-gamelog-residue.md,
-- restored everything that belonged on the pid it was deleted FROM. Nobody had
-- checked whether the games landed anywhere else. Mostly they did not.
--
-- DERIVATION, re-measured 2026-08-04 immediately before this file.
-- scratch/repair-name-match-misattribution/unowned-gamelog-inventory.sql reads
-- the 1,070 still-deleted rows out of gamelogs-residue-before.json, resolves
-- each game's rightful owner from nfl_play_stats on (esbid, player_name,
-- nfl_team) -- the same name key that misrouted the row in the first place,
-- which is why it finds the right player -- and checks player_gamelogs for that
-- owner at that esbid. 256 rows across 13 players have an owner who holds
-- nothing there. 57 carry real counting stats; 199 are roster-only.
--
-- PER-ROW OWNER MAPPING. The task entity's owner column is a min() aggregate
-- and indicative only; an early pass of this work mapped RASH-WALK-010501 to
-- GILB-BROW-007834, which is a different surname. Verified per row here:
-- every one of the 256 resolves to exactly ONE gsis id (no row has more than
-- one distinct candidate), and every resolved owner's last_name equals the
-- play-stat player_name's surname. Nothing was hand-waved through.
--
--   STEV-WEAT-023907 <- STER-WEAT-025072  132 rows ( 8 with stats)  Steve Weatherford (P, NO)
--   TERR-SMIT-011182 <- TREQ-SMIT-026877   30 rows (27 with stats)  Terrelle Smith (RB, NO)
--   JASO-FERG-006324 <- JAKE-FERG-027658   24 rows ( 0 with stats)  Jason Ferguson (DL, NYJ/DAL/MIA)
--   STEV-SMIT-011113 <- SHIX-SMIT-026046   22 rows (17 with stats)  Steve Smith Sr. (WR, CAR)
--   RASH-ANDE-010535 <- ROBB-ANDE-017101   19 rows ( 0 with stats)  Rashard Anderson (DB, CAR)
--   DHAN-JONE-009524 <- DANI-JONE-003986    6 rows ( 0 with stats)  Dhani Jones (MLB, NYG/PHI/CIN)
--   JERR-JOHN-008989 <- JOSH-JOHN-009443    6 rows ( 0 with stats)  Jerry Johnson (DL, DEN)
--   TYRO-DAVI-019548 <- TYLE-DAVI-002115    6 rows ( 5 with stats)  Tyrone Davis (TE, GB)
--   JAMM-BROW-015342 <- JORD-BROW-003929    5 rows ( 0 with stats)  Jammal Brown (OL, NO/WAS)
--   JONA-JENN-009780 <- JAUA-JENN-026160    2 rows ( 0 with stats)  Jonas Jennings (OL, SF)
--   MAUR-WILL-018965 <- MAXX-WILL-004748    2 rows ( 0 with stats)  Maurice Williams (OL)
--   COOP-TAYL-026661 <- CORE-TAYL-015520    1 rows ( 0 with stats)  Cooper Taylor (DB, NYG)
--   ROBE-FREE-001495 <- ROYC-FREE-006876    1 rows ( 0 with stats)  Rober' Freeman (DB, HOU)
--
-- Every owner clears player_could_have_played for every season written: the
-- narrowest margin is Steve Smith Sr. and Terrelle Smith at 22 and 23 in their
-- own rookie years, against a floor of 20. The team sequences corroborate the
-- identities independently of any identifier -- Dhani Jones NYG 2001-2003 /
-- PHI 2004-2006 / CIN 2007-2010, Jammal Brown NO 2005-2008 / WAS 2010-2011,
-- Jonas Jennings SF 2005-2008 -- all matching the real careers.
--
-- WHY A BACKUP REPLAY AND NOT A REGENERATION. The task planned to rebuild the
-- 57 stat-bearing rows with generate-player-gamelogs.mjs, on the reasoning that
-- the generator produces the row the generator would produce. Measured, it
-- cannot: 32 of the 57 are structurally unresolvable by it. Their nfl_play_stats
-- rows carry an EMPTY gsis_player_id and identify the player only through the
-- gsis id encoded inside smart_player_id, while the matching player row's own
-- smart_player_id was cleared by
-- db/adhoc/2026-08-04-clear-stolen-smart-player-id-encodings.sql. The generator
-- matches play stat -> player on those two columns directly and decodes
-- neither, so both lookups miss and it emits no row at all. Dry-run 2026-08-04
-- over five sample games: it produced a gamelog for the rightful owner in ONE
-- (Steve Weatherford, whose play stats do carry a gsis id) and for none of the
-- other four. Regenerating would also have meant running it across 56 whole
-- games, rewriting every other player's gamelog in them and running the prune's
-- DELETE over all of them -- far outside this task's 256 rows. A replay writes
-- exactly the 256 and nothing else. The generator's inability to decode
-- smart_player_id is a real defect and is recorded on the task; it belongs to
-- user:task/league/era-scope-player-name-matchers.md, not here.
--
-- SOURCE. All 256 backup rows read 'nfl-pro-gameday-roster' -- the dropped
-- column DEFAULT that db/adhoc/2026-08-04-drop-gamelog-source-default-and-
-- delete-prenatal-rows.sql established was never a writer stamp, so NULL is the
-- honest record and NULL is what this writes. Checked explicitly rather than
-- assumed: the backup carries a second value, 'nflverse-weekly-rosters', which
-- IS a real writer stamp, and NULLing it cost 154 stamps that had to be
-- recovered as league dc043c4bf. NONE of the 256 carries it.
--
-- COLUMNS THAT DO NOT TRANSFER. Three of the 106 describe the player rather
-- than the game and are corrected rather than copied:
--   pid          -- rekeyed to the rightful owner. That is the whole point.
--   pos          -- the backup holds the WRONG player's position on 11 of the
--                   13 (Weatherford's punts were filed under an LB, Terrelle
--                   Smith's carries under a WR). Set from the rightful owner's
--                   player.primary_position; all 8 distinct values are in the
--                   conformed position vocabulary the CHECK constraint enforces.
--   career_game  -- an index into the WRONG player's career. Written NULL.
--                   scripts/generate-player-career-game-counts.mjs owns this
--                   column and recomputes it for the whole table from the
--                   ordered gamelog set, so it refills on the next stats
--                   pipeline run. Note it must: inserting a rookie season under
--                   Steve Smith Sr. renumbers every later game he already has.
-- jnum is NULL on all 256 already. Everything else -- teams, counting stats,
-- active, started -- is a fact about the game or about the player who really
-- played it, and transfers unchanged.
--
-- GUARDED by NOT EXISTS on the primary key (esbid, pid, season_year) plus a
-- second guard on (esbid, pid) at ANY season_year, so a rerun, or a sibling
-- session that writes one of these rows first, is a no-op rather than a
-- duplicate. The trailing check RAISEs unless all 256 pairs are present, so a
-- guard that swallowed a row cannot pass silently.
--
-- Reviewed for scope: this file changes no `player` row (that is
-- finish-duplicate-person-cleanup's domain) and touches no column involved in
-- the in-flight boolean-prefix rename beyond `active`/`started`, which it
-- writes under their current production names.

